            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for kind words! And for opening an issue to discuss before actually making a PR. And for contribution suggestion.\r\n\r\nI am really not sure about this at the moment. Here are my thoughts:\r\n- The best way of buffer switching to me is indeed with `:Telescope buffers`.\r\n- The best way of buffer switching without dependencies is `:nnoremap <F5> :buffers<CR>:buffer<Space>` (taken from [here](https://vim.fandom.com/wiki/Easier_buffer_switching)). It will show all non-hidden buffers and prompt for buffer number input. It is very simple but really powerful. Not quite a selection with letters, but a very good simplicity/outcome trade-off.\r\n- I plan the 'mini.filetree' which will show file tree with possibility to open buffers. Not in the near future, but definitely is planned.\r\n- I also plan a module which will make some kind of opinionated settings and mappings. It will probably have mappings for `:bn` and `:bp`.\r\n\r\nSo all in all, every suggested functionality is either a very simple to add to personal config or planned in other modules. Lets leave this open for some time, I'll think more about it.",
