            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I think to estimate better the use cases, it would help to provide guidelines or a plugin how to create and read scratch buffers (not backed by file or stored in /tmp) for users and convert them to notes (backed by file).\r\nAnd to have a simple way to attach unique names (per cwd) to buffers + look them up.\r\n\r\nThe code is not particular complex, but having not return value from the uri functions is annoying, because it requires to store duplicates of all paths and loop through the current one:\r\n```lua\r\nM.makeScratch = function(scratchpath)\r\n  local uri = vim.uri_from_fname(scratchpath)\r\n  local bufnr = vim.uri_to_bufnr(uri)\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].bufhidden = \"\"\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].buflisted = true\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].buftype = \"nofile\"\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].readonly = false\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].swapfile = false\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- :ls! to list all bufs\r\n-- TODO: store and load scratch/notes files\r\n-- scratch -> notes (persistent)\r\n-- make neovim instance\r\nM.makeFileScratch = function(filepath)\r\n--M.makeNamedScratch = function(filepath, scratchname)\r\n  -- local bufs = vim.api.nvim_list_bufs()\r\n  --for i, v in ipairs(bufs) do\r\n  --  if(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(v) == \"abspath_tocompare\") then\r\n  --    print(\"matching comparison\")\r\n  --  end\r\n  --  print(k, \", \", v)\r\n  --end\r\n  local uri = vim.uri_from_fname(filepath)\r\n  local bufnr = vim.uri_to_bufnr(uri)\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].bufhidden = \"\"\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].buflisted = true\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].buftype = \"\"\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].readonly = false\r\n  vim.bo[bufnr].swapfile = false\r\n  return true\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nharpoon is basically this + storing and reloading as/from json with ~~the absolute path taken~~ usually the relative path unless outside of repo (then its absolute), a bunch of wrappers to send things to those buffers and doing this based on the numbering in 2 scratch buffers (files and terminals) [+ storing into backed file].\r\n\r\nI dont think json is necessary and sending stuff does not sound complicated either.\r\n\r\nUPDATE: fixed path explanation of harpoon",
