            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I think to estimate better the use cases, it would help to provide guidelines or a plugin how to create and read scratch buffers (not backed by file or stored in /tmp) for users and convert them to notes (backed by file).\r\n> And to have a simple way to attach unique names (per cwd) to buffers + look them up.\r\n\r\nI am not sure I follow.\r\n\r\nHere is the way to create new scratch buffer:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal new_scratch_buffer = function()\r\n  local buf = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(true, true)\r\n  vim.api.nvim_win_set_buf(0, buf)\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe idea is to quickly save scratch buffer to a file system? Like 'scratch_1' or 'scratch_2' in the current directory? After they are saved, I don't think they should be treated as scratch buffers.",
